For each product type $i$, the cost to buy $k$ units is $k^2 P_i$.
We want to maximize $\sum k_i$ subject to $\sum k_i^2 P_i \leq M$, where $k_i \ge 0$ are integers.
The constraints are:
$N \le 2 \times 10^5$
$M \le 10^{18}$
$P_i \le 2 \times 10^9$

Let $x_i$ be the number of units of product $i$ we buy. We want to maximize $\sum x_i$ subject to $\sum x_i^2 P_i \leq M$.
